      "pins": ["NAVC1.19", "NAVC1.32", "NAVC1.48", "NAVC1.64", "NAVC1.18", "NAVC1.63", "NAVC1.58", "NAVC1.59", "NAVC1.16", "NAVC1.17"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "GND", "I2C1_SCL_NAVC", "I2C1_SDA_NAVC", "UART2_TX_NAVC", "UART2_RX_NAVC"],
      "observed": "NAVC1 (STM32F405RGTx) VDD pins 19, 32, 48, 64 are on unconnected nets; VSS pins 18 and 63 are on Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18) instead of GND; I2C1 pins (e.g. PB6/PB8) are unconnected while I2C1_SCL_NAVC and I2C1_SDA_NAVC connect only to sensors, pull-ups and test points; UART2 and GPIO pins are similarly unconnected while their nets exist between the two MCU sides.",
      "expected": "NAVC1 must be powered from +3V3, grounded to GND, and connected to its I2C sensors, UART2 inter-MCU link, and GPIO signals as described in the specification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"92\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"VSS\")) (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"63\") (pinfunction \"VSS\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"36\") (name \"I2C1_SCL_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"R28\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"8\")) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"1\")) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The NAVC MCU is completely non-functional: it receives no power, has no ground reference, and cannot communicate with the sensors or the FCC, so the flight control system cannot perform navigation.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["FCC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.6", "FCC1.11", "FCC1.20", "FCC1.21", "FCC1.27", "FCC1.50", "FCC1.75", "FCC1.100"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "VREF+_FCC", "VDDA_FCC"],
      "observed": "FCC1 (STM32H753VITx) VDD pins 11, 27, 50, 75, 100 and VBAT pin 6 are on unconnected nets; VDDA pin 21 and VREF+ pin 20 are unconnected. The net named VREF+_FCC instead connects to FCC1 pin 13 (PH1), which is not the VREF+ pin.",
      "expected": "FCC1 must be powered from +3V3, with VDDA and VREF+ connected to the 3.3 V rail, and VREF+ must use pin 20 as defined by the STM32H753 pinout.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"165\") (name \"VREF+_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"PH1\")) ... (node (ref \"C30\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FCC MCU receives no power on its digital and analog supply pins, so it cannot boot or operate; additionally the VREF+ net is miswired to a GPIO pin, preventing proper ADC reference operation.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.1"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V"],
      "observed": "PCA9685PW address pin A0 (U2 pin 1) is tied to the +3.3V rail.",
      "expected": "A0 should be tied to GND to set the I2C address to 0x40 as stated in the specification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A0\") (pintype \"input\")) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The PCA9685 responds at I2C address 0x41 instead of 0x40, so firmware expecting 0x40 will not control the PWM/servo outputs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple severe anomalies: the NAVC and FCC MCUs are not connected to power/ground and many of their peripheral pins are left unconnected, and the PCA9685 address pin A0 is tied high, changing its I2C address from the specified 0x40 to 0x41."
}

